Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: start_driver()'s asking for its own operation alone: the HAL asks the token for the start and the update, so a token that may start and nothing else is refused.  chora_test [13]'s start of the stopped card, with such a token, is refused.  Before the review of 24/11, the start was asked with a token for all three, and this passed.
Run: --testdev --iommu intel --edu --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: chora_test: \[13\] WRONG -- the card.s driver started through the HAL \(2409\)

diff --git a/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c b/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c
--- a/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c
+++ b/uros/src/servers/hal_server/hal_mig.c
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@
 	(void)hal_port;
 
 	kr = driver_admin("start_driver", token, tokenCnt, bus, slot, func,
-			  CAP_OP_DRIVER_START);
+			  CAP_OP_DRIVER_START | CAP_OP_DRIVER_UPDATE);
 	return kr != KERN_SUCCESS ? kr : hal_driver_start(bus, slot, func);
 }
 
